# Short Thoughts

- When a tile is created, it has a set of starter values. Based on these the Manhatten distance is calculated to the nearest tile type. If the distance is less then a threshold, the tile becomes that type. If it is a specific type, it will start to influence its neighbors and might generate resources. By playing cards, the player can nudge tile values and cause them to evolve.

- Maybe the UI should move to the side of the table you're closest. So that if you move around the table, it's always somewhat in front of you.

- Maybe use an UV animator to animate a texture on the highlight to make it a bit more interesting.
